      correct:"B",tag:"MC-MAND-04",
      scaffold:"IB Paper 2 vocabulary-in-context questions require: (1) an accurate gloss of the word/phrase, AND (2) evidence that you understand it in context — not just a dictionary definition. 强制 (qiángzhì) = compulsory, forced, mandatory. 推行 (tuīxíng) = implement, roll out. Combined: mandatory implementation. Context: this tells us Shanghai residents were legally required to sort waste — it was not voluntary. Option A is too vague (no marks). Option C contradicts the text (市民起初觉得麻烦 shows it was not welcomed initially). Exam strategy: always anchor your answer to the sentence surrounding the word — 'the first city to MAKE this compulsory' is the contextual meaning.",
      reforge:{stem:"In the same article, 回收率提高了将近三成 — what does 将近三成 mean in context?",options:{A:"Exactly 30% — 三成 is a precise figure.",B:"Nearly 30% — 将近 (jiāngjìn) means 'almost', modifying 三成 (30%), so the rate rose by close to but not exactly 30%.",C:"About 3% — 三成 is misread as 三分.",D:"More than 30% — 将近 implies exceeding the figure."},correct:"B"}
